# Phylogeny exclusion mask for V. cholerae O1 2010EL-1786
# (CP003069.1 chr1, CP003070.1 chr2). BED: 0-based, end-exclusive.
#
# Regions excluded before building a core-SNP tree. 7PET is clonal --
# isolates differ by tens of SNPs genome-wide -- so a handful of spurious
# variants in repetitive or mobile sequence can dominate tree topology.
#
# Derived programmatically (2026-09-26) from the feature tables of the
# reference's own GenBank records, not from guessed coordinates:
#   rRNA    - rRNA genes (multi-copy operons: reads mismap between copies)
#   tRNA    - tRNA genes (short, repeated)
#   mobile  - CDS whose /product or /gene matches transposase, integrase,
#             phage, insertion sequence, IS<n>, recombinase or transposon
#   CTX_prophage_region - variable copy number and a recombination hotspot;
#             its presence is reported separately by the loci calls, so
#             excluding it from the tree loses no surveillance signal
#
# 144 merged intervals, 95,661 bp = 2.35% of the 4,077,740 bp reference.
# Regenerate by re-parsing the GenBank records if the reference changes.
#
#chrom	start	end	reason
